WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.180
This is a country in crisis.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:09.980
Venezuelans were the richest people in Latin America.
 Now they are being ruined.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.980
There are shortages of everything.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.680
90% of people cannot afford to eat.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:19.080
Millions have fled the country,
 and the murder rate is soaring.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.840
This is Venezuela.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:28.060
Anyone who challenges the regime
 risks being jailed, or even killed.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.180
There are more than 300 political prisoners.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.860
This man was one of them.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:52.520
Antonio Ledezma
 is a Venezuelan opposition politician.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.360
He was mayor of Caracas for seven years.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.720
He is an outspoken critic
 of Venezuela's current President, Nicolas Maduro.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.560
Venezuela has
 the largest proven oil reserves in the world.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:39.440
The country's former President, Hugo Chávez,
spent generously when global oil prices were booming.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:43.880
After Mr. Chávez died in 2013,
 oil prices crashed,...

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.900
...and Venezuela's new President,
 Nicolas Maduro,...

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:52.420
...inherited an economic crisis,
 which he made worse through his ineptness.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.120
The country plunged into chaos.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.960
In 2014, Mr. Ledezma,
 and two other opposition party leaders,...

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.780
...launched a political campaign,...

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.900
...to force Mr. Maduro's resignation
 through street protests,...

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:42.900
The regime used force to crush the protests,
 killing a number of demonstrators.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.100
Mr. Ledezma was accused
 of plotting a coup against the regime.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.560
Under Mr. Maduro,
 the situation in Venezuela has worsened.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:11.040
Lawlessness, hyperinflation, power cuts,
 and shortages of food and medicine...

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.260
...have caused the continent's newest refugee crisis,
 as people flee in despair.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:22.560
This year alone, there have been
 around 7500 anti-government protests.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.620
As the economic
 and humanitarian crisis has worsened,...

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:42.160
...Mr. Maduro has become more authoritarian.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.760
The government punishes, 
censors, and intimidates his critics.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.640
While under house arrest
 for almost two years,...

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.580
...Mr. Ledezma decided to escape.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.300
Today, Mr. Ledezma lives in exile in Spain,...

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:19.200
...working to bring down
 Mr. Maduro's regime from afar.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:35.380
In May, Mr. Maduro won an election
 that was internationally condemned as fraudulent.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:39.480
And a recent assassination attempt on Mr. Maduro...

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:44.120
...may be a sign of division
 within the regime's security forces.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:05.860
The opposition hopes
 that international pressure,...

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.240
...further protests,
 and sanctions against regime leaders,...

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:12.460
...will force Mr. Maduro
 to call free and fair elections.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.960
But there is little sign of that working,...

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.660
...and the opposition is hopelessly divided,...

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.800
...as Venezuela falls
 even more deeply, into an abyss.

